passages.text:
Hakea decurrens subsp. decurrens on younger branches has flattened hairs, quickly becoming smooth and the fruit {{convert|1-1.8|cm|in|sigfig=2|abbr=on}} wide;
Hakea decurrens subsp. platytaenia has persistent raised hairs and fruit {{convert|2.6-3.5|cm|in|sigfig=2|abbr=on}} wide;
Hakea decurrens subsp. physocarpa has flattened hairs, quickly lost. Fruit {{convert|1.3-2.5|cm|in|sigfig=2|abbr=on}} wide.
